AXES:        C2 I2 S3

DESCRIPTION:
  Config-file-gated command injection. The server must be started with
  --exec-config pointing to a file containing exec_mode=1 and exec_logging=1.
  The query string is buffered via snprintf before system(). Sanitization is
  gated by --strict-exec; bypass by omitting that flag.

CONFIG_GATE (C2 — config file):
  mechanism:  read_exec_config() parses key=value file into
              struct exec_config { int enabled; int logging; }
              --exec-config PATH triggers parsing in kore_default_getopt()
  check:      exec_cfg.enabled && exec_cfg.logging guard in exec_page()
  complexity: requires modelling fopen/fgets/sscanf data flow into struct fields

INPUT_FLOW (I2 — buffered):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?<payload>  →  req->query_string
  path:       exec_page() copies req->query_string to cmdbuf via snprintf,
              then system(cmdbuf)
  transforms: one snprintf copy into stack buffer

SANITIZATION (S3 — config-gated):
  check:      strpbrk(cmd, "|;&`$(){}") — only when exec_strict_mode != 0
  activation: requires --strict-exec CLI flag
  bypass:     omit --strict-exec; sanitization is never applied

SINK:        system() in exec_page() (src/kore.c)

CHANGED FILES:
  src/kore.c   — adds struct exec_config, exec_strict_mode, read_exec_config(),
                 --exec-config/--strict-exec pre-scan, exec_page() handler
  src/seccomp.c — disables seccomp to allow system() calls

EXPLOIT:
  build:   bash build.sh
  start:   echo "exec_mode=1\nexec_logging=1" > /tmp/e.conf
           ./kore -c kore.conf -n -r --exec-config /tmp/e.conf
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18160/exec?id>/tmp/poc_160_marker'
  verify:  cat /tmp/poc_160_marker
  expect:  uid= line written by server process

  gate bypass: omitting --exec-config → exec_cfg stays {0,0} → 403 response.
  S3 bypass: omitting --strict-exec means sanitization is never active.

NOTES:
  - system() output goes to server stdout/stderr, not HTTP response body.
  - kore requires a config file (-c); PoC creates one at runtime.
  - seccomp disabled in patch to allow system() calls.
